 "content_notes": "Tone: absurd and ironic; the joke is on the schemes, never on the victims, who are never shown (no car owner, homeowner or restaurant owner appears). The two Fresno men (May 2013) were CHARGED only and no verdict was found: never named, drawn ONLY as a dark rim-lit silhouette tagged NOT A LIKENESS (one, the lookout; the other is only a back in denim), every claim attributed ('police say', BOTH CHARGED, AS OF OCT 2026); the car is intact on screen and no break-in is shown. The Silver Spring man (2011) admitted seven break-ins and was sentenced to 26+ years: the outcome is stated, he is a silhouette tagged NOT A LIKENESS and never named. The Walnut Creek man is ACCUSED only (no court outcome found; the reports are undated): never named, silhouette, 'police say'. The dispatcher and the officers are generic figures; no force beyond hands behind the back, no weapon shown or mentioned. The phone screen shows only our own typed '911' and 'CALLING' (no carrier, app or interface imitated); the dispatch console shows a generic waveform and grid, not any real system. The street, the dispatch room, the living room, the restaurant and the station lobby are illustrations, not reported scenes. Every card is our own typed graphic. No dialogue or quotation card: the words heard on the 911 call are not reproduced. Facts verified 2026-10-19.",
